<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104985" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίκλῑν-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with three couches,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάλαμοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Moschio
				</span></i>
			 ap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				5.207c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. οἶκοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ath.
					2.47f
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				6.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίκλινος</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶκος</span>), ὁ, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				114
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1573.29
			</span></i>, <u>Gloss.</u>; also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίκλινον</span></b> , τό, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				1097.29
			</span></i> (Athens, <span class="entity">iv B. C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Anaxandr.
				70
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arched.
				2.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				30.26.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				388 ii 21
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>:— <i>dining-room with three
				couches,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συναγαγὼν τρεῖς ὄντας εἰς τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antiph.
					299
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. συγγενείας</span> a family <i>party,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Men.
				923.1
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅλον τ.</span> (acc.) a whole
				<i>dinner-party,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.71
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Anaxandr.
			</span></i> l. c., <i><span class="en">
				Arched.
			</span></i> l. c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>set of three couches,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐχ ὑποστρώσεις τ.;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Amphis
					46
				</span></i>
			, cf. <u>SIG</u> l. c., <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
			</span></i> l. c., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Caes.</u>
				55
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1277.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				23
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίκλινος ἤτοι ὡρεῖον</span> a
				<i>barn</i> (?) or a granary, <i><span class="en">
				Hero
			</span></i>
			<i>*Stereom.</i><i><span class="en">
				1.46
			</span></i>.</div>
